# Native Assets dashboard contract (7 October 2026)

## Evidence (7 October 2026)

- The existing AssetsService.mjs owns archive, restore (LOAD), unload and recover; do not create a second queue or archive engine. Its snapshot exposes project.jobs, sync errors and workspace.state, loadedCount, releasedBytes, recoverableCount. (7 October 2026)
- POST /api/assets-workspace, configured port 3100, accepts loopback only, application/json and x-zr-assets-client: 2. x-zr-auth is required only when the daemon has a nonempty ZENRAY_API_SECRET. BridgeClient.mjs already reads the local secret without printing it. Daemon.mjs explicitly starts with an empty API secret; this is a local client-header boundary, not proof of secret authentication. (7 October 2026)
- Action list returns all project snapshots; status with projectId returns one snapshot. Read these through BridgeClient.requestAssets directly: Client.mjs intentionally prints only id/sync/jobs and loses workspace fields. Do not read persisted files as live queue truth. Jobs exist in the service Map; service restart invalidates that runtime history. (7 October 2026)
- Jobs contain id/projectId/type/state, timestamps, error and optional progress/count/freedBytes/remainingCount. States observed in source: queued, running, done, error, interrupted. Archive and restore overwrite job.progress with their latest child-process event. (7 October 2026)
- Archive transfer events carry cumulative envoyes and bytes for the latest confirmed push, plus rail. chunk done/total measures local chunk preparation; progress seen/total measures scanned files; manifests done/total measures publication; verify total/ko measures verification. These are different units and cannot be presented as one upload percentage. (7 October 2026)
- Installed font files include /Users/zenray/Library/Fonts/AnthropicSerif-Regular.ttf and Light.ttf. Exact CoreText PostScript names and the drawn result still need runtime verification. Swift is available from Xcode. Existing native NSStatusItem patterns are in ZenRayDictate/AppDelegate.swift; the Cloud Electron tray is another application with its own engine and must not become a second Assets controller. (7 October 2026)

## Minimal implementation (7 October 2026)

- Build one accessory macOS Swift/AppKit application: NSStatusItem in the menu bar, NSPopover with a small project list, operation, state, last check time and error. Keep all visible UI and numbers in verified AnthropicSerif; fail visibly when the font is absent instead of silently claiming correct typography. Centralize sizes, intervals, executable/repository paths and labels. (7 October 2026)
- A tiny Node adapter imports BridgeClient.mjs, calls requestAssets({action:'list'}), projects only safe dashboard fields and writes JSON to stdout. Swift executes the configured Node executable with fixed arguments, no shell interpolation. Secret stays inside the adapter request header; never print env files, request headers, child environment or raw credentials. (7 October 2026)
- Poll asynchronously every 2 seconds while visible or a queued/running job exists; every 10 seconds when idle. One in-flight request only, bridge timeout bounded, no automatic restart/install action. On error show Service unavailable and last successful check; retain last data labelled stale, disable operation buttons and retry the same service. (7 October 2026)
- Sort active jobs first, keep projects segmented by stable projectId, show all active jobs rather than only snapshot's selected active job. Archive is Upload, restore/recover are LOAD, unload is UNLOAD. Show workspace loaded/unloaded independently from backup state. A request returning queued is acceptance, never completion. (7 October 2026)
- Spinner with phase text is correct when no meaningful denominator exists. Explicit file count is acceptable for progress seen/total. Explicit chunk byte count is acceptable for chunk done/total with label Preparing file. Confirmed transfer bytes may be displayed with label Uploaded, without assuming full-job total. No ETA or simulated rate. Because the latest event may hide intermediate transfers, do not derive network rate from this current snapshot. (7 October 2026)
- If continuous byte tracking is required, add a service-owned per-job telemetry accumulator which records phase, cumulative confirmedTransferBytes, updatedAt and operation identity separately from latest progress. It must survive later phase events and reset per job. Even then sampled confirmed-push rate is an acknowledged-push average, not instantaneous network throughput. Native client cannot manufacture missing measurements. (7 October 2026)
- Initial dashboard can be read-only with Open workshop through the existing server action. If LOAD/UNLOAD controls are included, use load-plan/unload-plan and server checks, submit restore/unload by projectId without custom filesystem deletion, then observe that job and refreshed workspace until terminal. Disable duplicate submission. Errors remain visible and retry requires an explicit click. (7 October 2026)

## Verification gates (7 October 2026)

- Adapter fixtures: running archive, restore, unload, queued, error, interrupted, absent progress, missing fields, service unavailable, stale snapshot, simultaneous jobs and same project names with distinct IDs. Assert no queued acceptance or stale done event produces a success claim. (7 October 2026)
- Progress fixtures: chunk versus transfer versus manifests versus verify must retain their units. Missing denominator yields indeterminate state; NaN/negative/oversized counters are rejected. A failed verify cannot render as uploaded and verified. (7 October 2026)
- Native build and model test: compile via SwiftPM; unit-test decoder/state mapping and deterministic sorting; runtime check NSFont and screenshot the actual popover in light/dark mode. Ensure close does not terminate Assets service. (7 October 2026)
- Live proof: read current list via adapter, compare projectId/jobId/workspace to direct requestAssets output without printing credentials. Exercise an isolated test project for queued/running/done/error and LOAD/UNLOAD with original production sources retained. Stop or deny the bridge in a fixture to verify visible unavailable state; no destructive live outage is required. (7 October 2026)
- This audit changes no production file and installs nothing. Native UI, telemetry and runtime appearance are requirements, not completed work. (7 October 2026)
